# Federation 0.0.187 — direct remote transcode + access that actually hides
# Branch: feature/direct-play-and-access (worktree ~/Documents/jf-direct), base origin/master 0.0.186
# Legend: [ ] todo  [~] in progress  [x] done  [!] blocked/needs decision
# Details, reasoning and evidence live in notes.md.

## 0. Baseline
[x] Worktree from origin/master 0.0.186 (user runs 0.0.186)
[x] Baseline plugin tests: 960/960 pass
[x] Clone Jellyfin server/web v12.0 source for reference (scratchpad, read-only)

## 1. Remote transcode handoff (client <-> owner, receiver keeps session)
### Owner side (server that has the media)
[x] Config: RemoteServer.AllowRemoteTranscode (default true), PluginConfiguration.EnableRemoteTranscodeForFriends (default true), MaxRemoteTranscodesPerFriend (0 = unlimited)
[x] PlaybackToken response advertises remoteTranscode capability for this caller
[x] Gateway route Peer/Play/{token}/{**nativePath}
    [x] strict allowlist of native paths (HLS master/main/segments, progressive stream, universal audio, subtitles, attachments)
    [x] item id in path must equal token item; media source id must belong to item
    [x] token re-validated every request (friend exists, enabled, item visible to that remote user)
    [x] loopback relay, internal key in header only, never in query, strip ApiKey/api_key/token params
    [x] playlist rewrite: every URI line + URI="" attribute -> absolute gateway URL, credentials stripped
    [x] CORS (echo Origin, no cookies), Range passthrough, cancellation, no retry splicing
    [x] concurrency limit per friend by distinct PlaySessionId (429 when exceeded)
[x] Control route: ping + stop for play sessions this token started (bound, not guessable)
### Receiver side (server the user is logged into)
[x] Token client parses remoteTranscode flag; grant cache (user, source) -> server, remote item, token, capability
[x] Provider: capability-aware source description (no capped progressive MP4 when peer can transcode; force transcode when over WAN cap)
[x] Filter: HLS master/main -> fetch from owner, rewrite to absolute owner URLs, serve; fallback to local on any failure
[x] Filter: progressive transcode/universal audio/segments -> 302 to owner gateway
[x] Filter: subtitles/attachments -> fetched from owner (no whole-file pull through receiver)
[x] Strip receiver ApiKey from forwarded params; clamp VideoBitrate to friend WAN cap
[x] Mixed-content guard (https page never handed http owner URLs); scheme check like existing static redirect
[x] Session bridge: PlaybackProgress -> ping owner (throttled), PlaybackStopped -> stop owner job
[x] Admin UI: Advanced → "Who converts friends' video" card (+ per-friend status), Friends tab per-friend switch
[x] Unit tests: RemoteTranscodeHandoffTests (31), FederationVisibilityServiceTests (14)

## 2 + 3. Access that hides, not just blocks playback
[~] Live config has zero rules: fixture save path works ("Saved.", delivered). Remaining suspect: admin UI flow — check in browser
[x] Pull model: Peer/UserRules endpoint; receiver fetches its rules from each friend every sync (push stays as fast path)
[x] Visibility tag service: per local user hidden tag, stamped on every hidden federated item (+ series/season/episodes), user policy BlockedTags maintained
    [x] recompute after sync, on rule receipt, on startup; diff-only writes; remove tag when rule cleared
    [x] covers Blocked / CertainLibraries / CertainItems / BlockedItemIds / per-user rating ceiling
[x] Sharing change on owner -> notify friend (CatalogChanged) -> friend resync prunes libraries no longer shared
[x] Verify sync prunes a library that disappears from Peer/Libraries (not treated as transient)
[x] Rule delivery status: superseded by the pull model (every sync pulls the friend's rules)
[x] Unit tests + two-server smoke (federation_peer_smoke.py) pass on 12.2

## 4. Validation + release
[x] Full gate on frozen commit 72c5c61: 1006 plugin + 170 Companion + 116 UI tests, twice, receipt written
[x] Two-server fixtures on frozen commit: peer smoke 5/5 (12.2), handoff smoke 6/6 on 12.2 and 12.0
[x] Version 0.0.187: csproj, meta.json, manifest (md5 2e033381b2395192f46d0cbbdce02dbd), zip = DLL+meta+logo+thumb
[x] Commit, merge to master, push, GitHub release (0.0.187)
[x] Deploy to live server (user's) — 0.0.187 Active on Jellyfin 12.2.0


# ======================================================================
# Federation 0.0.188 — friends' favorites + downloads to device
# Branch: feature/favorites-and-downloads, base origin/master 0.0.187
# ======================================================================

## 5. Downloads to device (any user, any app)
Root cause: Jellyfin only offers Download for local files (CanDownload = IsFileProtocol);
a federated item's Path is a URL, so web/Android/Findroid/Swiftfin hide Download and
/Items/{id}/Download throws. The web-only "Download to device" menu entry handed the
browser a loopback (127.0.0.1) URL and refused any title with a per-user rule.
### Owner side
[x] DirectStream download=true: Content-Disposition attachment with the real file name (RFC 6266 filename*)
[x] Token response advertises deviceDownload=true for Download tokens
[x] Viewer-bound download tokens: own limit per viewer (not the friend-wide 3/hour server-copy limit)
[x] Peer/UserRules also reports friend-level allowDownloads + shareFavorites
### Receiver side
[x] Store what the friend allows (PeerAllowsDownloads, PeerSharesFavorites); preserved by config Save
[x] /Items/{id}/Download filter: user, visibility, friend rule, source online -> viewer-bound Download token
    -> 302 straight to the friend (same scheme, new friend) or relay through this server (old friend / scheme change)
[x] Error answers carry the friend's reason (not allowed / limit reached + Retry-After / offline)
[x] CanDownload=true in item responses for federated videos/audio the user may download
[x] Web: drop the broken injected "Download to device" entry (native Download now works); DownloadUrl returns the native path
[x] Tests: decision logic, filename header, CanDownload rules, token cache
## 6. Friends' favorites
Design (user picked): each friend shares which of its own titles its users favorited —
anonymous, only titles already shared with you; your Favorites tab gets "Favorites on <friend>".
[x] Owner: Peer/Favorites — favorites of enabled local users, own media only, visible to the calling viewer, ranked, capped, cached
[x] Owner setting ShareFavoritesWithFriends (default on)
[x] Receiver: FriendFavoritesService — pull per friend per viewer (cached), map to local items, filter by viewer visibility
[x] Receiver: /Plugins/Federation/FriendFavorites (signed-in user) -> sections per friend
[x] Receiver setting ShowFriendsFavorites (default on)
[x] Web: per-friend sections below the native Favorites sections (native card look, no gradients)
[x] Admin UI: both switches in Advanced
[x] Tests: aggregation, ranking, mapping, visibility, settings
## 7. Validation + release
[x] Gate twice on frozen commit
[x] Two-server fixture: device download (redirect + relay), CanDownload, friends' favorites section data
[x] Version 0.0.188 (zip md5 4c4e574dfe8a4c0b208635b99775ce4a), release, master
[x] Deploy live: 0.0.188 Active on Jellyfin 12.2.0, startup sync 0 ERR (backup plugin-backup-federation-0.0.187-20261019)


# ======================================================================
# Federation 0.0.189 — federated watch parties (SyncPlay with friends)
# Branch: feature/watch-parties, base origin/master (0.0.188 + deploy record)
# ======================================================================
User: "group watch party at the same time watching the same federated media… at the top you
usually create a group watch party, but with this you click on that but can make one with
federation friends."

## 8. Design (details in notes.md)
[x] Each server keeps a normal SyncPlay group; a hidden link session (custom ISessionController) relays. Host = hub.
[x] Friends' viewers see the party in /SyncPlay/List and join natively via /SyncPlay/Join.
[x] Titles matched per server (owner id / federated copy / provider ids); SyncPlay + friend rules still apply per viewer.
[x] Loading: remote "Wait"/"Go" makes the host hold; host loading pauses friends; never mutual waits.
[x] Host heartbeat every 5 s corrects drift; links drop after 60 s silence; host holds a joiner at most 30 s.
## 9. Build
[x] Wire DTOs, item mapper, link rules (PartyLink), link controller, FederatedPartyService
[x] Peer endpoints Peer/Party/Announce, Peer/Party/{id}/Join|Leave|Event
[x] Viewer endpoints Party, Party/Share, Party/Status/{groupId}; settings Settings/WatchParties (+ Advanced card)
[x] SyncPlay List result filter + Join action filter
[x] Web: "New group with friends" / "Invite friends" / "Watching with ..." in the SyncPlay menu
[x] Unit tests: WatchPartyTests (22) + 4 web tests
[x] Two-server smoke federation_party_smoke.py: 8 stages, passed 3 runs in a row
    Bugs found by it and fixed: Jellyfin sends no message when a group loads from idle into
    paused (link now reads the group's real state, polls while a joiner loads); loading pauses
    were relayed as user pauses (now Wait/Go); stale pause after resume (state confirmed first);
    a Ready<->"pause when ready" loop (~1000 requests/run, now ~40); Jellyfin 12 sockets need ApiKey=.
## 10. Validation + release
[x] Gate twice (1047 plugin, 170 Companion, 124 web); peer 7/7, handoff 6/6, party 8/8; older friend 0.0.188 and 0.0.187 pass
[x] Version 0.0.189 (zip md5 050d90d62a385abd7371cbb3bef0fee3), release, master
[x] Deploy live: 0.0.189 Active on Jellyfin 12.2.0, startup sync 0 ERR (backup plugin-backup-federation-0.0.188-20261020)


# 0.0.190 — download destination, friends' viewers on dashboard, playback connection info, transcode placement
## 1. Server download destination
[x] Pick where a server download goes: an existing library (default: Movies for films, Shows for episodes) or a new folder (becomes its own library)
[x] Movies land as "Name (Year)/Name (Year).ext", episodes as "Series/Season NN/Series SNNEMM.ext" so the library identifies them
[x] Paths confined to the chosen library's folders; partial files never deleted outside them
## 2. Friends' viewers on the owner's dashboard
[x] Receiver reports start/progress/stop of its viewers' federated plays to the owner (throttled)
[x] Owner shows each as a session (title, position, paused, play method, "bob (friendflix)"), ends it on stop or silence
[x] Settings: share our viewers with friends; show friends' viewers
## 3. Playback Info: federation connection section
[x] Endpoint describing the connection for a play session (friend, route, who converts, latency, friend's hardware)
[x] Web: extra "Federation" block in the player's Playback Info panel
## 4. Transcode placement by hardware (optional, off by default)
[x] Servers share transcode hardware (auto from Jellyfin encoding settings, or manual for offloaded transcoding like ours)
[x] Receiver picks owner vs itself against per-quality minimums; owner stays the default
## 5. Validation + release
[x] Unit tests (34 new) + web tests (9 new); gate 1081 plugin / 170 Companion / 133 web
[x] Two-server on 12.2: peer 9/9 (new: friends' viewers on owner dashboard, Playback Info, hardware, download destinations), handoff 6/6, party 8/8, older friend on 0.0.189 6/6
[x] Release 0.0.190 (zip md5 9cb488c7c77baf8ba9cdd67702c399da), master
[x] Deploy live: 0.0.190 Active on Jellyfin 12.2.0, startup sync 888 items 0 ERR (backup plugin-backup-federation-0.0.189-20261020)
## 6. Later (user asked: review only, do not implement)
[x] Review the svoeth fork (github.com/svoeth/JellyfinFederationPlugin/releases): what it adds, what we already have, what could be useful. User has their own thoughts before anything is built.
    Read 2026-10-20 (release notes only, no code pulled). Their 0.0.177-0.0.186 are our own releases.
    From 0.0.187 (15-19 Oct) they number their own work 0.0.187-0.0.196, colliding with ours
    (their 0.0.190 != our 0.0.190) -> confusing if anyone mixes catalogs.
    Already have (ours, often more complete): change notices between friends, retry/resume downloads,
      per-library sync status, background refresh, removal held over two syncs, path-escape fix on
      server downloads, "friends watching your titles" (ours: native dashboard sessions, 0.0.190),
      new-friend prompt choosing libraries.
    New to us, possibly useful (NOT built; user wants to discuss first):
      - Per-friend privacy: friends see your users only if you share them ("Users they can see")
      - Choose which of your friends each friend can discover (friends-of-friends control)
      - Sharing end date (whole friendship or per library)
      - Per-friend limits: simultaneous streams, monthly data
      - "Preview what they see" (owner views the catalog as a given friend gets it)
      - Usage tab: per-friend totals, most-watched titles; playback in Jellyfin's activity log
      - "Popular on <friend>" collection from shared play counts (like our friends' favorites)
      - Reconnect: renew keys from a new request at the same address, keep libraries/settings;
        auto-replace the server's own internal key when Jellyfin stops recognising it (one-way 503s)
      - Full resync button per friend library; safer library removal during a sync
      - Music: 416 on range -> fetch whole file; albums/artists synced with songs; type change moves songs
      - "Cannot access a disposed object" when saving settings during a sync (check we don't have it)
      - Large removals (>25 titles and >10%) wait for admin confirmation
